. Marcitentan, used for pulmonary hypertension, is also metabolized by CYP3A4, with variants *2, *3, *4, *5, *8, *10, *15, *16 having 102–504% higher activity, *7, *14, *18, *28–*32 having 50%-91% lower activity, and *9, *11-*13, *17, *20–*24, *33, *34 showing 5–45% lower activity (
Li et al., 2019
). Saxagliptin, an anti-diabetic medication, is metabolized by CYP3A4 to 5-hydroxy saxagliptin, with variants *11, *12, *17, *20, *23 having 1.91–7.90% lower clearance, *2 showing 10% lower 5-hydroxy saxagliptin formation, and *3, *4, *7, *8, *9, *13, *16, *18, *24, *29, *31, *32, *34 having 24.16–45.38% lower clearance, and *5, *10, *14, *19, *28, *33 classified as a mild reduction group (
Liu et al., 2022
).
