). Istradefylline, an A2A receptor antagonist for Parkinson’s, is metabolized by CYP3A4, with *29 showing increased activity, *2, *3, *14, *31, *32 having 50–90% of wild-type activity, and *33, *34 having 35–38%, while *17 is nearly inactive (
